From 77e456ec9b75570be2c4b3083108f816627fb8d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allcodernet <67543055+allcodernet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:43:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/45] decide: option-order debiasing and temperature

A request with order_debias K gets K_eff = effective_variants catalogue
variants: slot v holds variant v's prefix (resident, restored from the prefix
cache or built), state c owns K*(1+B) sequence ids from seq_base + K, variant
v's trunk at offset v*(1+B) with its branches after it (K = 1 is the old
layout). Each variant runs the same branches in the same phases; per field the
K distributions are averaged (order_spread, mean coverage), then temperature
(options.temperature, else --decide-temperature) is applied with
apply_temperature + rebuild_answer. Dependent fields use the lines of these
answers in every variant. The sequence budget and its 400 message count K
prefix slots; the per-state cell message names K_eff for K > 1.
Response: engine.order_debias and engine.temperature, scored_tokens x K;
dump: tokens.prefixes and a variant on every entry; info: seqs_per_state and
states_per_round for the body's K. The order_debias and temperature guards are
removed. Model-free helpers in decide-debias (layout, budget, temperature,
variant combination) with test-decide-debias.
